---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="What To Do If You're Between Bra Sizes: Band & Cup Rounding | BraSizeChecker"
  description="Practical advice for measuring between bra sizes. Learn how to handle odd underbust numbers (31, 33), half-cup differences, and hook adjustments."
  canonical="https://brasizechecker.com/guides/between-bra-sizes"
>
  <Header />
  <main class="flex-1 w-full max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-8 sm:py-12 md:py-16">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[
      { label: 'Guides', url: '/#guides' },
      { label: 'Between Bra Sizes' }
    ]} />

    <header class="mb-10 text-center sm:text-left">
      <span class="inline-block py-1 px-3 rounded-full bg-canvas-soft-2 border border-hairline text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-primary mb-3">
        Evergreen Guide
      </span>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-ink tracking-tight mb-4">
        What To Do If You're Between Bra Sizes
      </h1>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 text-xs text-mute mb-4">
        <span>By BraSizeChecker Editorial Team</span>
        <span>&bull;</span>
        <time datetime="2026-08-24">Updated August 2026</time>
      </div>
      <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-body leading-relaxed max-w-3xl">
        Human bodies don't naturally come in exact 2-inch increments. If your underbust falls on an odd number (like 31 or 33 inches) or your bust falls between cup letters, here is how to find a comfortable fit.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="space-y-10 text-body leading-relaxed text-sm sm:text-base">
      <section class="bg-surface border border-hairline rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8">
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-ink mb-4">1. Odd Underbust Measurements (e.g., 31" or 33")</h2>
        <p class="mb-4">
          Standard US and UK bra bands are manufactured in even numbers (30, 32, 34, 36). If your underbust measures 31 or 33 inches:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-xs sm:text-sm mb-4">
          <li><strong>Round Up to Nearest Even Band:</strong> In modern direct underbust sizing, round up to the nearest even number (31 underbust &rarr; 32 band).</li>
          <li><strong>Test Sister Sizes:</strong> Test both your baseline rounded size and your smaller sister size (e.g. try both 32D and 30DD with a bra extender if needed).</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="bg-surface border border-hairline rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8">
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-ink mb-4">2. Between Cup Letters</h2>
        <p class="mb-4">
          If your bust-to-band difference falls on a half-inch (e.g., 3.5 inches difference between C and D):
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-xs sm:text-sm mb-4">
          <li>Choose stretch-lace cups that conform to half-cup variations without gaping.</li>
          <li>Fit the larger breast if your breasts are asymmetrical, using removable cup pads for the smaller side.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="bg-surface border border-hairline rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8">
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-ink mb-4">3. Helpful Tools</h2>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
          <a href="/#calculator" class="px-5 py-2.5 bg-primary text-white font-bold text-xs rounded-xl hover:bg-primary-hover shadow-2xs">Re-Calculate Size &rarr;</a>
          <a href="/sister-size-calculator" class="px-5 py-2.5 bg-surface border border-hairline text-ink font-semibold text-xs rounded-xl hover:bg-canvas-soft-2 shadow-2xs">Sister Size Tool &rarr;</a>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
